{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>From the wing.</b> It is possible that the meaning is that they are the righteous, and because the earth is round he said מכנף הארץ (from the wing of the earth), and the meaning is from a distant place." "<b>צבי (glory).</b> Splendor, or from the Aramaic translation, and the word ואומר (and I say) refers to every nation, and so we have heard." "<b>רזי.</b> From the root of וישלח רזון בנפשם (Psalms 106:15), and the meaning is twice in every moment." "<b>Treacherous ones have dealt treacherously.</b> For every man is treacherous ones; one treachery after another."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:59.744903777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}